# Admin sidebar: 3-level nesting

WordPress `add_menu_page` / `add_submenu_page` is **2 levels only**. Do not invent a third PHP menu API.

## Levels

1. **08600 Solution** — `add_menu_page` slug `08600-dashboard`
2. **Group or leaf** — Dashboard (leaf); Waybills / Trips / Customers / Operations / System (groups)
3. **Pages** — still registered with `add_submenu_page` so caps, URLs, and `current` highlighting stay core

## Canonical map

`kit_admin_menu_nesting_groups()` in `includes/admin-menu-nesting.php`. JS only transforms `#toplevel_page_08600-dashboard .wp-submenu`.

| L2 | L3 slugs |
|---|---|
| Dashboard | `08600-dashboard` (ungrouped leaf) |
| Waybills | `08600-waybill-create`, `08600-waybill-manage`, `warehouse-waybills` |
| Trips | `08600-trip-create`, `kit-deliveries` |
| Customers | `08600-customers`, `08600-customer-portal-accounts` |
| Operations | `route-management`, `08600-countries`, `manage-drivers` |
| System | `08600-settings`, `08600-sync-runs`, `08600-help` |

Hidden pages (`parent` `null`) stay out of the sidebar.

## Rules

1. New visible pages: `add_submenu_page('08600-dashboard', …)` **and** add the slug to the map (or leave ungrouped).
2. Flatten a group when fewer than 2 children are visible (caps hide Settings / Sync Runs).
3. Match WP admin chrome — no custom colour scheme, cards, or gradients on `#adminmenu`.
4. Inline (expanded + current): accordion, current group open. Flyout (hover / folded): L3 opens to the right.

```text
Bad: add_submenu_page('08600-waybill-create', …) hoping for a third WP level
Good: register under 08600-dashboard; add slug to kit_admin_menu_nesting_groups()
```
